      "genre": "travel article",
      "title": "GETTING AROUND AMSTERDAM BY BICYCLE",
      "source_label": "travel guide",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Are you visiting Amsterdam? The most popular way to travel in the city is by bicycle. Amsterdam is flat and small, so it is easy to ride. There are more bicycles than people in the city."
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "The first bicycles in Amsterdam were heavy and expensive. Only rich people had them. Now bicycles are cheap, and almost everyone has one. The city built special roads for bicycles. These roads are separate from the roads for cars."
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Before you ride, you should know the rules. Cyclists must stop at red lights. You should use your hand to show drivers you want to turn. Most people are friendly and will help you if you are lost."
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "You do not need to buy a bicycle. Many shops rent bicycles by the hour or by the day. The price is about ten euros a day. Ask the shop for a lock, because thieves often take bicycles."
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "If you do not want to ride, there are other choices. Trams are fast and clean. Buy your ticket before you get on. Say 'Dank u wel!' to the driver. This means 'Thank you!' in Dutch."
        }
      ],
      "stats": {
        "word_count": 187,
        "paragraph_count": 5
      }
    }
